+# CONTRACT — Versioned Document Store with Structural Merge
+
+Definition of done. Every box must pass via the vitest suite (`npm test`), a clean `tsc` build, and clean `npm run lint`.
+
+## Documents (CRUD)
+- [ ] `create(id, content)` stores a new document → test: `get(id)` returns deep-equal content
+- [ ] `create` throws if ID already exists on current branch → test: second `create` same id throws
+- [ ] `create` allows re-create after `delete` → test: delete then create succeeds
+- [ ] `create` throws if content is not a plain object (array/primitive) → test: `create('x', [])` throws
+- [ ] `get(id)` throws if document doesn't exist → test: `get('nope')` throws
+- [ ] `get(id)` throws if document was deleted → test: delete then get throws
+- [ ] `get` returns a deep clone (mutating result doesn't affect store) → test: mutate returned obj, re-get unaffected
+- [ ] `create` deep-clones input (mutating input after create doesn't affect store) → test: mutate input obj, get unaffected
+- [ ] `update(id, content)` replaces content → test: get returns new content
+- [ ] `update` throws if document doesn't exist/deleted → test: update missing throws
+- [ ] `delete(id)` removes document → test: subsequent get throws
+- [ ] `delete` throws if document doesn't exist/deleted → test: delete missing throws, double delete throws
+
+## Version History
+- [ ] `create` generates a version; `update` generates a new version each time → test: history length grows
+- [ ] versions have unique `id`, numeric `timestamp`, full `content` → test: ids unique, timestamp is number, content matches
+- [ ] `getHistory(id)` returns versions chronological (oldest first) → test: timestamps non-decreasing, contents in order
+- [ ] `getHistory` throws for missing doc → test: throws
+- [ ] `getVersion(id, versionId)` returns content at that version → test: returns historical content (clone)
+- [ ] `getVersion` throws for unknown versionId / wrong doc → test: throws
+
+## Branching
+- [ ] default branch is `"main"` → test: `getBranch()` === 'main'
+- [ ] `createBranch(name)` branches from current branch's current state → test: docs visible on new branch
+- [ ] `createBranch(name, fromBranch)` branches from given branch → test: state matches fromBranch
+- [ ] `createBranch` throws if name already exists → test: throws
+- [ ] `switchBranch(name)` changes active branch → test: getBranch reflects; throws if unknown
+- [ ] changes on one branch not visible on another → test: create on branch, not on main
+- [ ] `listBranches()` returns all branch names → test: contains created branches
+
+## Merging
+- [ ] one-sided field change is taken with no conflict → test: applied true, value merged
+- [ ] both sides same field same value → no conflict → test: applied true
+- [ ] both sides same field different value → conflict → test: applied false, conflict reported with path/base/ours/theirs
+- [ ] no conflicts → auto-applied (`applied:true`) and current branch updated → test: get reflects merge
+- [ ] conflicts → not applied (`applied:false`), current branch unchanged → test: get unchanged, conflicts returned
+- [ ] `merged` always contains result; conflicts resolved in favor of ours → test: merged shows ours value at conflict
+- [ ] merge with no changes on either side is a no-op (fast-forward) → test: applied true, no version churn
+- [ ] different documents changed on different branches merge cleanly → test: no conflict, both changes present
+- [ ] nested/structural merge: non-overlapping nested fields merge cleanly; overlapping differing → conflict with dotted path → test: `a.b.c`
+- [ ] array fields treated atomically (both change differently → conflict; one changes → taken) → test
+- [ ] delete on one side, unchanged on other → deletion applied → test
+- [ ] delete on one side, modified on other → conflict (path "") → test
+- [ ] document created only on source branch is brought in → test
+- [ ] re-merging after a clean merge is a no-op → test: second merge applied true, no new conflicts
+- [ ] merge throws if source branch unknown → test: throws
